-- A field's options are lifted into the section the record is declared in,
-- so they are section-local exactly as the record is
-- (specs/proposals/INLINE-ONE-OF-FIELD-SPEC.md §5.8). Two sections may each
-- declare a `Plot` with a `tenure`: the lifted types are
-- `Plots`.`Plot's tenure` and `Leases`.`Plot's tenure`.

§ `Plots`

DECLARE Plot HAS
    `tenure` IS ONE OF Owner, Tenant, Lodger

GIVEN p IS A Plot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`owned` p MEANS p's tenure EQUALS Owner

§ `Leases`

DECLARE Plot HAS
    `tenure` IS ONE OF Owner, Manager

GIVEN t IS A `Plot's tenure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`managed` t MEANS t EQUALS Manager

§ `Use`

-- From a third section, the section names which `Plot's tenure` is meant.
GIVEN t IS A `Plots`.`Plot's tenure`
GIVETH A STRING
`label` t MEANS
  CONSIDER t
  WHEN Owner THEN "owner"
  WHEN Tenant THEN "tenant"
  WHEN Lodger THEN "lodger"

#ASSERT `Plots`.`owned` (`Plots`.Plot WITH tenure IS Owner)
#ASSERT `managed` Manager
#ASSERT `label` Lodger EQUALS "lodger"
